DEFERRED FOLLOW-UP, PREREQUISITE TO ISSUE #17 (porting providers), NOT a delta to the vision 'the surface is three verbs and a selection'. Human directive, recorded verbatim in substance.

PROBLEM, as the human sharpened it: the existing RUNTIME registry is NOT the main problem. DEFAULT-PROVIDER BOOTSTRAPPING is. Measured at origin/main before m9: rivretrieve._internal.discovery._ensure_default_providers_registered is 151 lines comprising a 13-clause boolean early-return guard followed by 13 near-identical 'if <id> not in registered' blocks, each doing a local import of that provider's module, loading its packaged catalogue artifact, and calling _registry.register. Adding provider 14 requires edits in three places (the guard clause, a new registration block, and its import), and omitting the guard clause silently costs a re-registration scan on every call. The only genuine per-provider variation is small: exactly 2 of 13 providers pass engine_provider_module (usgs_nwis, ca_eccc) while the rest pass provider_module=None, and all 13 provider modules already define _CATALOGUE_PATH.

SOLUTION SPACE DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN. Package iteration is NOT adopted and must not be assumed. The follow-up must COMPARE an explicit declarative built-in-provider manifest against package discovery and justify the choice. The human explicitly does NOT want implicit import-time registration, and does NOT want filesystem scanning, without justification. One manifest entry may be safer than making the package layout an implicit registry. The orchestrator's earlier suggestion that 'registration iterates the providers package' was premature and is superseded by this directive.

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA the follow-up must satisfy, as dictated by the human:
1. adding a provider requires no changes to discovery.py;
2. provider ID, catalogue location, and observation-engine capability are declared once;
3. registration is deterministic and idempotent;
4. duplicate IDs, missing catalogues, and malformed declarations fail loudly;
5. a test proves that a newly declared provider becomes discoverable and routable;
6. built-in registration remains explicit enough to audit.

NON-GOAL, explicitly downgraded by the human: 'one new directory and zero central files' is DESIRABLE BUT NOT MANDATORY, and must not be treated as a constraint that forces package discovery.

SEQUENCING: deferred until milestone m9 of the current vision has landed, because m9 rewrites discovery.py substantially and two cross-milestone union collisions have already occurred in this run. Route through /to-vision after the current run completes, as a prerequisite to issue #17.
